Step 3 (knowledge base update, line 8): This step updates the knowledge base S, which is simple as each task is from a distinct domain in this paper. That is, the set of extracted aspects is simply added to the knowledge base S for future use. We will not discuss Step 1 and step 3 further as they are fairly straightforward. Our focus is on the two recommendation methods, which will be introduced in Section 4.4.4. For the recommendations to work, we first need to learn the past knowledge in terms of word vectors WV and association rules AR. We discuss knowledge learning next.
