4.5 LIFELONG-RL: LIFELONG RELAXATION LABELING
Shu et al. [2016] proposed a lifelong relaxation labeling method called Lifelong-RL, which incorporates LML in the relaxation labeling method [Hummel and Zucker, 1983]. LifelongRL was applied to a sentiment analysis task. This section gives an overview of Lifelong-RL. We first introduce the relaxation labeling (RL) algorithm. We then briefly describe how to incorporate the lifelong learning capability in RL. For the application to the sentiment analysis task, please refer to the original paper.
4.5.1 RELAXATION LABELING
